<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The human built stasis container as it is found rather than built. Behaves like the one the
		player crafts - claim it, use it, uninstall it and haul it home, or deconstruct it back into
		its steel, plasteel and spacer components - but it comes with an occupant sealed inside, so
		it is its own def and nothing else places it.

		Footprint is 2x2; the prefab reserves a third row so the tall sprite is not drawn into a wall.

		North only. A PrefabDef with no rotations declared resolves to All, and the container's
		graphic is a single 2x3 sprite on a square 2x2 footprint, so an East or West placement turns
		the sprite on its side and leaves the container lying down. Vanilla declares the same one
		rotation on every prefab whose art only reads one way up.

		The chance is what keeps a large complex from filling with them. Each of the three rooms this
		is injected into takes at most one, so the count follows the number of rooms rather than the
		size of the complex, and a 9800 point mechanitor complex has enough of them to hand the
		player fifteen. Three in ten placements keeps that closer to four or five without changing
		which rooms they turn up in.
	-->
	<PrefabDef>
		<defName>APM_MechanoidStasisContainer</defName>
		<rotations>North</rotations>
		<size>(2,3)</size>
		<things>
			<APM_MechanoidContainer_Ancient>
				<chance>0.3</chance>
				<position>(0, 0, 0)</position>
			</APM_MechanoidContainer_Ancient>
		</things>
	</PrefabDef>

</Defs>
